# Route split: HTTP actions (anything the CLI or a browser calls by path) live
# on the backend under /http/, and the Convex API and file storage at its root.
# Getting this split wrong fails silently — the request reaches a port that
# answers, just not the route that knows it.
#
# HTTP actions go to 3210 with the /http prefix added HERE, never to the
# backend's site port (3211). That port is `dev_site_proxy`
# (crates/local_backend/src/proxy.rs): it adds the same prefix and forwards to
# 3210, through a service hard-coded to 4 requests at a time. At ~13 HTTP
# actions a second, with model calls holding a slot for 10s, every request
# behind it queued: 2026-10-13 the same action answered in 0.1s on
# 3210/http and in 5 to 17s on 3211, for every `cast` command, webhook, sign
# in and published page.
#
# TLS: convex.codecast.sh is DNS-only in Cloudflare, NOT proxied (verified
# 2026-09-13: no cf-ray, server: railway-hikari). Clients therefore talk to this
# origin directly and need a PUBLICLY TRUSTED certificate — a Cloudflare Origin
# CA certificate would be rejected, because only Cloudflare's proxy trusts those
# and there is no proxy in the path.
#
# The certificate must exist BEFORE cutover, and an HTTP challenge cannot supply
# it: HTTP-01 requires the hostname to already point here, which is only true
# after the switch. So this uses a DNS challenge, which proves control through a
# DNS record instead. That needs a Cloudflare API token with DNS:Edit on the
# codecast.sh zone in CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, and a Caddy binary built with the
# caddy-dns/cloudflare module — the stock binary does not include it.
{
	admin off
	acme_dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
}

convex.codecast.sh {
	@http_actions path /.well-known/* /api/auth/* /api/github-app/* /api/webhooks/* /cli/*
	handle @http_actions {
		rewrite * /http{uri}
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3210
	}
	handle /api/storage/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3210 {
			header_down Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
		}
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3210
	}
}
